        <i class="bi bi-calendar-event"></i> International Seminar on Flexible Transport (DRT)
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted mb-4">
        <i class="bi bi-geo-alt text-success me-1"></i> Council Hall, Province of Asti, Piazza Alfieri 33 &nbsp;&nbsp;
        <i class="bi bi-calendar3 text-success me-1"></i> 24 January 2011, 8:30 am
      </p>

      <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #475569;">
        It is increasingly evident that traditional public transport in low-density areas is far less competitive than the private car. The International Seminar on Flexible Transport addressed the question: <em>is there a way to make public transport more efficient, more flexible and closer to the needs of citizens?</em>
      </p>
      <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #475569;">
        The seminar examined application, planning and organisational aspects of flexible transport (demand-responsive transport), drawing on real-world experiences from Italy, Scotland, Switzerland and South Africa.
      </p>

